actice he is in  breach of his contract and does not get  paid nfl policy is that helmets have to  be certified by  n-o-s-c-a-e they don't certify equipment  that's older than 10 years that in a  nutshell is the problem and you pointed  out during break we didn't even get to  this in the first segment the idea that  antonio brown at one point took his old  helmet and tried to paint it with the  raiders colors and sneak it onto the  field that's how far this has come this  is the level of zaniness that we are  dealing with here and i have no idea  chris where it's gonna go from here no  absolutely no idea and uh that pretty  you know it's good to see the nfl put  that statement out there that's gonna  quiet a lot of the noise and i think  that's what we can expect to hear from  the arbitrator about the case from  antonio brown when when the time comes i  mean there's just no ground to stand on  especially this day and age where we're  talking about player safety we're not  just going to let a player i don't give  a damn if it's antonio brown peyton  manning just do whatever he wants and  antonio brown can quit football antonio  i mean peyton manning retired and man  the nfl ratings were still amazing and  gosh peyton manning is about as big as  it ever came in  as sorry as a star in the nfl so antonio  brown if he wants to do all this crap  he's not going to win this battle and  the other thing other thing mike you  know you talked about the planning of  the seeds with john gruden right and you  know when will be that time where he can  take no more i'll tell you when it'll be  when antonio brown can't deliver for his  offense anymore that'll be the big issue  as soon as there's slippage there that's  when you'll see things really go bad but  as long as antonio brown starts to carve  people up in otas and training camp and  still has you know uh all his physical  ability he's gonna have the backing of a  guy like john gruden because john gruden  believes in him and w